# Your exported Claude Code usage stays on your machine.
#
# tools/export-usage.py writes here. The file contains token counts, session
# counts and the names of directories you have worked in — it is your data,
# and the published site is public, so it is not committed by default.
#
# If you deliberately want it published, force it:  git add -f assets/data/usage.json
assets/data/usage.json
